      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain how lisinopril actually works in the raas pathway? i need to understand the specific steps for my exam",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Lisinopril, an ACE inhibitor, works by blocking the conversion of angiotensin I to angiotensin II through inhibition of the angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE). This results in decreased angiotensin II concentration, leading to vasodilation and a reduction in blood pressure. It also reduces aldosterone secretion, decreasing water and sodium retention which further helps to lower blood pressure. Additionally, lowering angiotensin II levels helps to reduce the afterload, making it easier for the heart to pump. This comprehensive effect makes lisinopril effective for treating hypertension and heart failure.",
      "source": "target",
